---
// About: personal page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, social } from '../data/site';
const facts = [
  { label: 'Also known as', value: site.alias },
  { label: 'Works in', value: 'Watercolor, ink, gouache, acrylic, and occasionally pixels' },
  { label: 'Draws', value: 'History, myth, religion, fable and literature' },
  { label: 'Lives and works in', value: 'Tennessee Appalachia' },
];
---
<Base title="About" description={site.intro} image="/images/about/jordan.jpg">
  <div class="page">
    <section class="intro">
      <figure class="photo"><img src="/images/about/jordan.jpg" alt="Jordan Holt" width="1236" height="1400" fetchpriority="high" /></figure>
      <div class="txt">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Jordan Holt</h1>
        <p class="lede">{site.intro}</p>
        <dl>{facts.map((f) => <div><dt>{f.label}</dt><dd>{f.value}</dd></div>)}</dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story">
      <div class="block">
        <h2>A bit about me</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>I spent the bulk of my career in higher ed, teaching illustration, graphic design, art history and theory. As of late I’ve scaled down my teaching to spend more time in the studio.</p>
          <p>I have an MFA in illustration from Academy of Art University. Years of professional experience in graphic design. Experience self-publishing and working with publishers, and the better part of two decades working with clients as a freelance illustrator.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <h2>In the studio</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>My work is almost exclusively traditional methods. Dominantly I work in watercolor and ink, but I’ll experiment with just about any method when I can, and I’ve got a real desire to get back into oil someday.</p>
          <p>I spent more than a decade working mostly digitally, but shifted away from that process in 2023 for <a href="https://youtu.be/huQ5o44hWqI?si=wdzPO6nZbHNxLvBc" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="u">reasons I explain in this video</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <h2>Teaching</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>I began teaching as a full-time art professor in 2015, and was tenured in 2021. In 2026 I took a formal leave of absence from teaching to spend a year in the studio, where I am now. We’ll see what the future holds. In the meantime <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@jholtillus" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="u">I also talk about art on my YouTube channel</a>.</p>
          <p>As part of my teaching life I’ve led many trips to Italy, and I still try to go every year if I can.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block">
        <h2>Outside the studio</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>My wife and I married when we were 20. And in the nearly 2 decades since we’ve had 6 children. We live in a little hollow surrounded by woods in rural East Tennessee, which we’re trying to build up into a (very) small farm.</p>
          <p>As I’ve aged my values have crystalized. An experiential faith in Christ, doggedly pursued, is the source of the good in my life. Through that, and depending on how well I’m doing that, I view my family, my work, and the natural world in which I live. I’m interested in old things that don’t change frantically around me. Politics and current issues disinterest me, and I want to engage primarily with the old and trustworthy.</p>
          <p>Reading great literature feeds great creativity, as does the experience of nature. Languages are beautiful and thought provoking. Playing music brings color to life.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <figure class="studio"><img src="/images/about/fire.jpg" alt="A fire at dusk in the woods" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" /></figure>

    <section class="end">
      <div>
        <h2>Say hello</h2>
        <p class="muted">For commissions, publishing or just to talk shop. You can also find me on {social.slice(0, 3).map((s, i) => <>{i > 0 && (i === 2 ? ' and ' : ', ')}<a href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="u">{s.label}</a></>)}.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact/" class="btn solid">Start a conversation</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 1fr) 1.3fr; gap: clamp(28px, 6vw, 96px); align-items: center; }
  .photo { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; margin: 0; overflow: hidden; background: var(--soft); }
  .photo img, .studio img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .txt h1 { margin: 16px 0 20px; }
  .txt .lede { margin-bottom: 32px; max-width: 46ch; }
  dl { margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  dl div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 150px 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 14px; }
  dt { color: var(--muted); } dd { margin: 0; }
  .story { margin-top: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px); display: grid; gap: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .block { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr; gap: clamp(16px, 5vw, 80px); padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .block h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.2rem); }
  .copy { max-width: 62ch; }
  .copy p { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .studio { aspect-ratio: 21 / 9; margin: clamp(64px, 9vw, 112px) 0 0; overflow: hidden; background: #111; }
  .studio img { object-position: 50% 60%; }
  .end { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 24px; margin-top: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px); padding: 40px 0 96px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .end h2 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .end p { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .intro, .block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .photo { max-width: 420px; } .studio { aspect-ratio: 3 / 2; } dl div { grid-template-columns: 124px 1fr; } }
</style>
